.TH MU2EDAQ_SHIFTER_TOOLS_CONFIG 3 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq_shifter_tools.config \- configuration discovery, loading and precedence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B from mu2edaq_shifter_tools import config as cfg
.B from mu2edaq_shifter_tools.config import Operations, ConfigError
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This module centralises every configuration decision the toolkit makes.
Its counterpart on the shell side is
.BR daq-common.sh (3),
and the two implement the same precedence and the same search path so
that a shell command and a Python command resolve a setting
identically.
.SH PRECEDENCE
Every setting resolves as
.PP
.RS
command line > environment > .env > config file > default
.RE
.PP
.BR resolve ()
implements exactly that and is what the command line tools feed their
parsed options into.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Precedence
.TP
.BI resolve( "cli=None, env_var=None, dotenv=None, config=None, config_key=None, default=None, environ=None" )
Return the first tier that supplies a value. \fIcli\fR is the parsed
option, or \fBNone\fR when it was not given. \fIenv_var\fR names an
environment variable, consulted in \fIenviron\fR (default
\fBos.environ\fR, injectable for tests). \fIconfig_key\fR is a dotted
path into \fIconfig\fR.
.IP
An empty environment value is treated as absent, so an
exported-but-empty variable does not mask the lower tiers. A falsey
\fIcli\fR value such as \fB0\fR is respected, since zero is a
legitimate port offset.
.SS Locations
.TP
.BI repo_root()
The installation root: \fB$MU2EDAQ_ROOT\fR if set, else the first
ancestor of the package containing
\fIconfig/daq\-operations.example.yaml\fR, else
\fI~/daq\-shifter\-tools\fR.
.TP
.BI config_search_path()
The directories searched for config files, in order, de-duplicated:
\fB$MU2EDAQ_CONFIG_DIR\fR, \fI./config\fR, \fI<root>/config\fR,
\fI~/.config/mu2edaq\fR, \fI/etc/mu2edaq\fR.
.TP
.BI find_config_file( "name, explicit=None" )
Locate a config file by name. \fIexplicit\fR is used as-is with
\fB~\fR expanded and is required to exist. Raises \fBConfigError\fR
naming the whole search path when nothing is found.
.TP
.BI data_dir()
The static data directory: \fB$MU2EDAQ_DATA_DIR\fR or
\fI<root>/data\fR.
.TP
.BI data_file( "name" )
Path to a data file, e.g. \fBdaq_nodes.json\fR. Raises
\fBConfigError\fR if absent.
.SS Loading
.TP
.BI load_config( "path" )
Load a YAML file and require a mapping at the top level. JSON loads
too, being a subset of YAML. An empty file yields \fB{}\fR.
.TP
.BI dotenv_files( "explicit=None" )
The \fI.env\fR files to read, highest precedence first:
\fB$MU2EDAQ_DOTENV\fR, \fI~/.mu2edaq/env\fR, \fI<root>/.env\fR,
\fI./.env\fR. Only existing files are returned.
.TP
.BI find_dotenv( "explicit=None" )
The highest-precedence \fI.env\fR file, or \fBNone\fR.
.TP
.BI load_dotenv( "explicit=None" )
Parse every file from \fBdotenv_files()\fR into one dict, with an
earlier file's value winning. Lines may carry an \fBexport\fR prefix
and one layer of matching quotes; blanks, comments and non-identifier
keys are ignored.
.IP
This deliberately does
.B not
touch \fBos.environ\fR. The caller passes the result to
\fBresolve()\fR, which ranks it below the real environment; mutating
the environment would invert that.
.TP
.BI load_tunnels( "explicit=None" )
Load the tunnel definitions, accepting either a bare list or a mapping
with a \fBtunnels:\fR key. Each entry must carry \fBhostname\fR and
\fBport\fR.
.SH CLASSES
.SS Operations
Typed accessors over the operations configuration.
.TP
.BI Operations.load( "explicit=None" )
Classmethod. Locate and load the operations YAML, honouring
\fB$MU2EDAQ_CONFIG\fR and then the \fI.env\fR files.
.TP
.BI Operations( "data, path=None" )
Wrap an already-parsed mapping, which is what the tests do.
.PP
Instance attributes and methods:
.TP
.B path
The file the configuration came from, or \fBNone\fR.
.TP
.B data
The parsed configuration as a plain dict.
.TP
.BI partitions()
Configured partition names.
.TP
.BI partition( "name" )
One partition's configuration. Raises \fBConfigError\fR listing the
known names.
.TP
.BI environments( "partition" )
Every environment defined in a partition.
.TP
.BI environment( "partition, name" )
One environment's configuration. Raises \fBConfigError\fR listing the
known names.
.TP
.BI active_environments( "partition" )
The partition's \fBactive_environments\fR, defaulting to every defined
environment when the key is absent. A bare string is accepted as a
one-element list.
.TP
.BI base_release( "partition" )
The partition's base release path.
.TP
.BI test_rel_path( "partition, environment" )
The environment's test release directory.
.TP
.BI setup_cmd( "partition, environment" )
The environment's setup command, arguments included.
.TP
.BI ots_port_offset( "partition" )
The partition-wide ots port offset; 0 if unset.
.TP
.BI port_offset( "partition, environment" )
The environment's offset within its partition; 0 if unset.
.TP
.BI gateway_port( "partition, environment" )
\fBots_port_offset\fR + \fBport_offset\fR, which is how ots derives the
port.
.TP
.BI resource_manager_port()
The ResourceManager port; 1973 if unset, Mu2e being E-973.
.SH EXCEPTIONS
.TP
.B ConfigError
Raised for missing, unreadable or inconsistent configuration. Messages
name the file and, where a lookup failed, the values that were
available. The command line tools catch it and exit 1 with the message
on stderr.
.SH CONSTANTS
.TP
.B OPERATIONS_CONFIG
\fI"daq\-operations.yaml"\fR.
.TP
.B TUNNELS_CONFIG
\fI"tunnels.yaml"\fR.
.TP
.B ENV_PREFIX
\fI"MU2EDAQ_"\fR, the prefix of every variable the toolkit reads.
.TP
.B ROOT_MARKER
\fIconfig/daq\-operations.example.yaml\fR, the file that identifies an
installation root.
.SH EXAMPLES
Resolve a setting with the standard precedence:
.PP
.RS
.nf
from mu2edaq_shifter_tools import config as cfg

dotenv = cfg.load_dotenv()
partition = cfg.resolve(
    cli=args.partition,
    env_var=cfg.ENV_PREFIX + "PARTITION",
    dotenv=dotenv,
    default="partition_0",
)
.fi
.RE
.PP
Handle a configuration problem the way the commands do:
.PP
.RS
.nf
try:
    ops = cfg.Operations.load()
except cfg.ConfigError as exc:
    sys.exit(f"my-tool: {exc}")
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq_shifter_tools (3),
.BR daq-common.sh (3),
.BR daq-read-config (1)
